FirstMetOldDuke: {
	OldDukeName: Old Duke
	L0: ......
	L1: Sheathe your bloodlust, youngster. There is no need for swords to be drawn the moment we meet.
	L2: I am old. I have grown weary of such violent games.
	L3: We can cooperate.
	L4: I am collecting something special: Ocean Scraps.
	L5: If you can find more for me, I will make it well worth your while.
	L6: Here is a sample.
	B1: Have you changed your mind?
	B2: Farewell, then.
	HL1: The old professor...? Though, he doesn't seem to recognize me.
	HL2: His words are credible. We were colleagues at Sulphurous Sea University. He is a titan in the field of marine archaeology.
	C1: Accept cooperation
	C2: Refuse cooperation
	C3: Refuse and draw weapon
	C1Response: Excellent. I hope we have a pleasant partnership.
	C2Response: ...Then I shall take my leave. If you think it through, you are welcome anytime.
	C3Response: ...It seems you insist. Then let me measure your worth.
}

OldDukeCampsite: {
	OldDukeWanderingActor.InteractHint: "[Right Click] Talk"
	OldDukeCampsite.TitleText: Old Duke's Campsite
}

CampsiteInteractionDialogue: {
	GreetingLine: What do you require?
	Choice1Text: I am here to trade.
	Choice2Text: I brought the things you wanted.
	Choice3Text: Just wandering around.
	Choice4Text: I want to spar with you.
	Choice5Text: Tell me about your past.
	Choice2DisabledHint: Insufficient Ocean Scraps
	Choice1Response: See what I have here.
	Choice2Response: Good. These scraps are sufficient. This is your due reward.
	Choice3Response: ......
	QuestCompleteLine: Hmm... Do you have any new discoveries? I am very busy right now.
	B1: I will spend the next few days deciphering these scraps. I will notify you once I am finished.
	Choice4_R1: I may be old, but I haven't lost the skills of my youth.
	Choice4_R2: Then let us see if you have improved recently.
	Choice4_R3: Using me as a whetstone is not a wise move...

	CampsiteChatDialogue: {
		GreetingLine: Want to chat?
		Choice_BackToMain: Change topic
		Choice_EndConversation: That is all
		Choice_PastStory: About your current state
		Choice_Research: What are you piecing together?
		Choice_SulfurSeaHistory: The truth of this sea
		Choice_AboutFragments: About those fragments
		Choice_PersonalLife: You don't look so good
		Choice_Farewell: Goodbye
		Past_Intro: That is a past deliberately wiped away. Or perhaps, there are few fish left who know of it.
		Past_University: We were arrogant then, thinking we could measure the whole world with a ruler. Until we dug up something... illogical at the bottom of the abyss.
		Past_Prime: That thing could not be killed, nor destroyed. It was not a living creature.
		Past_Accident: There were no survivors in that incident. When I was being assimilated by that coldness, I made a manic decision.
		Past_Mutation: Since there was no escape, I joined it. I forced it into my body. Since then, I am not truly alive, nor can I die.
		Past_Exile: It is just as well. This body is strong enough to suppress this sea.
		Past_Reflection: I just want to guard this sea. If those things try to crawl out of the abyss, that will be the moment I risk total resurgence and death to stop them.
		Research_Intro: I am trying to reconstruct a story, or rather, recover a lost form of experience.
		Research_CurrentWork: These fragments cling to memories of the past. They record how that ancient civilization sought a path to survival in a desperate situation.
		Research_Breakthrough: To fight that kind of terror, brute force is useless. You must find their 'killing rules' and exploit them.
		Research_Difficulties: But deciphering them is dangerous. These fragments are conduits themselves. Stare at them too long, and you might hear sounds you shouldn't.
		Research_Theory: If I can assemble all the pieces, perhaps I can find a way to permanently seal the source of the abyss.
		Choice_Research_Details: What do you mean by 'killing rules'?
		Choice_Research_Help: What do I need to do?
		Choice_Research_Back: Sounds crazy
		Research_Details1: For example, there are things you cannot look at, names you cannot speak. Once a conduit is triggered, death is inevitable. That civilization tried to bind gods with rules.
		Research_Details2: They even built massive containers, attempting to imprison those things. Unfortunately, the containers leaked.
		Research_Help: Help me find more fragments. The rest of my life will be spent researching this.
		History_Intro: The Sulphurous Sea is merely a facade. This is the residue left after the encroachment of that thing's domain.
		History_Origin: This was once the Sapphire Sea, until the source went out of control.
		History_Civilization: That ancient civilization was powerful. They learned to utilize that eerie power. They built cities, like dancing on a powder keg.
		History_Cataclysm: Naturally, the balance broke. Some terror revived, and all living things were erased in an instant, becoming part of this dead silence.
		History_Ruins: What you see now is merely the residue after that event. The water changed color because it died. Completely died.
		History_Warning: If you ever see the dead waving at you, or hear familiar calls... remember, that is just this sea of corpses mimicking the living.
		Choice_History_MoreRuins: Where is the most dangerous place?
		Choice_History_Dangers: Are there any countermeasures?
		Choice_History_Back: Unsettling
		History_MoreRuins1: At the very bottom of that corpse sea. There is a door. Do not knock. Whatever is behind it had best rot in there forever.
		History_MoreRuins2: There are still unopened rooms in those sunken ruins. They are secret chambers cast from special heavy metals, designed to cut off the perception of those things.
		History_Dangers1: Aside from the mutated walking dead, beware of things you cannot see. Sometimes, the fatal strike is invisible.
		History_Dangers2: Do not trust your eyes. Do not respond to inexplicable calls. In that sea of corpses, the living are the anomalies.
		Fragments_Intro: Ocean Scraps... in my eyes, they are bloodstained archives.
		Fragments_Nature: They are the residue of a phenomenon. Like compressed curses.
		Fragments_Power: Each fragment is a 'conduit'. Alone, they may be harmless, but when enough gather, they create a collision of eerie forces.
		Fragments_Collection: They are scattered across every corner of the dead sea—some buried under ruins, others grown into the flesh of creatures.
		Fragments_Purpose: I am still piecing them together, trying to reconstruct the source of that disaster. Only by figuring out how that thing killed can I find a way to imprison it.
		Personal_Intro: Getting by.
		Personal_Daily: I spend most of my time sleeping to reduce fluctuations in my consciousness. If my emotions get too intense, the thing inside me gets... restless.
		Personal_Loneliness: Solitude is good. If it gets too lively around here, it must be because 'they' have come. I am used to being a lone fish. It is safer for me, and for the world.
		Personal_Memories: My memory is blurry. Sometimes I cannot tell which memories are mine, and which are... the memories of other individuals remaining in this body.
		Personal_Hope: Seeing you reminds me of myself back then. Ignorant and fearless. I hope you don't end up like me, turning yourself into this shape.
		Choice_Personal_Tea: What are you drinking?
		Choice_Personal_Past: Are you still considered... a fish?
		Choice_Personal_Back: Take care
		Personal_Tea1: This is brewed from several special plants in the abyss. The taste... is like rotting mud.
		Personal_Tea2: Want a cup? It will calm you down like a dead fish.
		Personal_Past1: Who knows? Maybe the real me died long ago, and what remains is... another kind of thing with his memories.
		Personal_Past2: But I still remember the feeling of sunlight on my face, the touch of books. As long as I remember these, I consider myself alive.
		Personal_Past3: If not for that accident... I would probably be lying peacefully in a grave by now. Instead of being like this, unable to die even if I wanted to.
		Farewell_Normal: Let's leave it at that. Come find me if you need anything.
		Farewell_Friendly: Be careful, youngster. In this world, a peaceful end is a luxury.
	}
}

FirstCampsiteDialogue: {
	L0: You've come.
	L1: I have been collecting these scraps for quite some years.
	L2: They are... peculiar. They do not look like products of natural evolution, but rather foreign objects that "invaded" this world.
	L3: I hope you understand what I mean. My intuition tells me they should have been formless things, merely choosing a form that Terrarian creatures could comprehend.
	L4: Regardless... I wish to decipher them, but I lack sufficient quantity.
	L5: I hope you can help me collect enough Ocean Scraps.
	L6: I will provide you with appropriate compensation.
}

ComeCampsiteFindMe: {
	B1: ...Come have a cup of tea when you have time.
	C1: I have business with you.
	C2: I was just fishing for fun...
	B1_NO: Come find me first. You'd best learn the path.
}
